          "what": "Run multiple coroutines concurrently",
          "why": "Test concurrent execution timing",
          "example": "python3 -c \"import asyncio; import time; s=time.time(); asyncio.run(asyncio.gather(asyncio.sleep(1), asyncio.sleep(2))); print(f'{time.time()-s:.2f}s')\"",
          "output": "2.00s",
          "explanation": "gather runs both sleeps concurrently — total time is max(1, 2) = 2s, not 3s. Demonstrates the power of concurrency",
