          "what": "Tokenize text and see individual tokens",
          "why": "Understand how tokenization works and count tokens",
          "example": "python3 -c \"from transformers import AutoTokenizer; t=AutoTokenizer.from_pretrained('gpt2'); ids=t.encode('Hello, world!'); print(f'Tokens: {len(ids)}, IDs: {ids}, Text: {t.decode(ids)}')\"",
          "output": "Tokens: 5, IDs: [15496, 11, 995, 0], Text: Hello, world!",
          "explanation": "Shows how text is split into tokens. Note: 'Hello, world!' becomes 4 tokens — punctuation and spaces are separate tokens",
